<h1>Interview Preparation for Freshers</h1>
<p>Preparing in advance can help you explain your qualifications, skills and career goals clearly during a job interview.</p>

<h2>1. Research the Company</h2>
<p>Visit the official website and understand its products, services, location and the role you are applying for.</p>

<h2>2. Prepare Your Introduction</h2>
<p>Example: “Good morning. I have completed my graduation and developed knowledge in my field through academic projects and practical learning. I am looking for an opportunity to apply my skills, learn from experienced professionals and contribute to the organisation.”</p>

<h2>3. Common Interview Questions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Tell me about yourself.</li>
<li>Why do you want to join our company?</li>
<li>What are your strengths?</li>
<li>What skills are relevant to this job?</li>
<li>Why should we hire you?</li>
<li>What are your career goals?</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Answering Questions</h2>
<p>Keep answers honest, clear and relevant. Use examples from college projects, training or previous work wherever possible.</p>

<h2>5. Documents to Carry</h2>
<ul>
<li>Updated CV</li>
<li>Education certificates and marksheets, if requested</li>
<li>Experience or training certificates, if applicable</li>
<li>Valid identity document, if requested</li>
<li>Interview invitation or contact details</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Interview Day Tips</h2>
<ul>
<li>Arrive on time.</li>
<li>Dress appropriately.</li>
<li>Listen carefully before answering.</li>
<li>Ask relevant questions about responsibilities and training.</li>
<li>Never pay money to guarantee a job offer.</li>
</ul>

